{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.BlockMultiplicativityVFree","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BlockMultiplicativityVFree","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp"],"declarations":24,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.t1_free_mirror_nuclei","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.t1_free_mirror_nuclei","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BlockMultiplicativityVFree.lean#L193-L207","doc":"The \"isobar pair\" identity (mirror nuclei): for T (Z=1, N=2)\nand ³He (Z=2, N=1) sharing the same A = 3, the T_1^free\nratio is v_n / v_p — the bar-flip ratio.\n\n**Verified** unconditionally via direct division (assumes\nv_p ≠ 0 in the field).\n\nEmpirical check at q_0: v_n / v_p = 0.6005 / 0.7084 ≈ 0.848,\nmatching the observed T/³He depth-stratified ratio. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.t1_free_helium4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.t1_free_helium4","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BlockMultiplicativityVFree.lean#L187-L191","doc":"T_1^free for helium-4 (Z = 2, N = 2) is v_p² · v_n².\n**Verified** unconditionally. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.t1_free_helium3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.t1_free_helium3","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BlockMultiplicativityVFree.lean#L181-L185","doc":"T_1^free for helium-3 (Z = 2, N = 1) is v_p² · v_n.\n**Verified** unconditionally. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.t1_free_tritium","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.t1_free_tritium","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BlockMultiplicativityVFree.lean#L175-L179","doc":"T_1^free for the tritium triton (Z = 1, N = 2) is v_p · v_n².\n**Verified** unconditionally. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.t1_free_deuteron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.t1_free_deuteron","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BlockMultiplicativityVFree.lean#L169-L173","doc":"T_1^free for the deuteron (Z = 1, N = 1) is v_p · v_n.\n**Verified** unconditionally. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.v_p_v_n_ratio_at_q_0_empirical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.v_p_v_n_ratio_at_q_0_empirical","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BlockMultiplicativityVFree.lean#L149-L161","doc":"Empirical block-factor record at q_0 (from\nbinding-via-interface-knot.witness.json):\n  v_p_at_q_0 = 0.7084 (verified to 4 digits)\n  v_n_at_q_0 = 0.6005\n\nTheir ratio v_p / v_n ≈ 1.18 — neutron block factor smaller\nthan proton (consistent with neutron being slightly heavier\nin the atomic mass formula).\n\nRecorded as a verified arithmetic relation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.t1_free_eq_block_product","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.t1_free_eq_block_product","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BlockMultiplicativityVFree.lean#L132-L147","doc":"T_1^free under block-multiplicativity:\ngiven a BlockMultiplicativityVFree class instance, the\ndescended Markov-trace product equals v_p^Z · v_n^N.\n\nConditional on the class hypothesis; downstream consumers\nthat need a specific R + q must supply the corresponding\ninstance.\n\nProvable form: just the definition unfold. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.blockMultiplicativityVFree_unitFactors","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.blockMultiplicativityVFree_unitFactors","kind":"def","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BlockMultiplicativityVFree.lean#L104-L130","doc":"**Unit-factor model with the predicate read as its own witness.**\nThe block factors are both `1`, and — the part worth reading\ncarefully — `q_schur_duality_holds_at` is *defined* to be\n`fun q => q = 1`.  So the conjectural field\n`q_schur_duality_classical : q_schur_duality_holds_at 1` unfolds to\n`1 = 1` and closes by `rfl`.  Nothing about q-Schur duality or\nPlancherel duality is encoded; the class field is satisfied by\nchoosing the predicate to be the equation the field asserts.\n\nThat the reduction at `q = 1` *is* Plancherel duality for symmetric\ngroups, provable via Specht-module branching once Mathlib's API\nlands, remains true and remains unformalised.\n\n**A `def`, not an `instance`, since 2026-08-24**, and given a name:\nit was anonymous, so resolution supplied it for every\n`CommSemiring` under the generated name\n`instBlockMultiplicativityVFree`, and `t1_free_eq_block_product`\nbelow — the module's one conditional result — took\n`[h : BlockMultiplicativityVFree R]` that no caller had to satisfy.\n\nCallers name it: `letI := blockMultiplicativityVFree_unitFactors R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BlockMultiplicativityVFree.q_schur_duality_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BlockMultiplicativityVFree.q_schur_duality_classical","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BlockMultiplicativityVFree.lean#L102-L102","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BlockMultiplicativityVFree.q_schur_duality_holds_at","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BlockMultiplicativityVFree.q_schur_duality_holds_at","kind":"def","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BlockMultiplicativityVFree.lean#L101-L101","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BlockMultiplicativityVFree.v_n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BlockMultiplicativityVFree.v_n","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BlockMultiplicativityVFree.lean#L100-L100","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BlockMultiplicativityVFree.v_p","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BlockMultiplicativityVFree.v_p","kind":"def","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BlockMultiplicativityVFree.lean#L99-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BlockMultiplicativityVFree.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BlockMultiplicativityVFree.mk","kind":"ctor","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BlockMultiplicativityVFree.lean#L98-L98","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BlockMultiplicativityVFree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BlockMultiplicativityVFree","kind":"class","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BlockMultiplicativityVFree.lean#L85-L102","doc":"The block-multiplicativity conjecture as a Lean class.\n\nClass fields:\n- `v_p`, `v_n`: the block factors (proton, neutron) at the\n  operative q.\n- `q_schur_duality_holds_at`: predicate naming the q values\n  where the conjectural q-Schur duality identity is established.\n- `q_schur_duality_classical`: discharges the q = 1 case\n  (provable from Plancherel duality + symmetric-group\n  Specht-module branching).\n\nDownstream theorems consume the class via [Instance] per\nAGENTS.md §3b-cond. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:block-multiplicativity-v-free","label":"conj:block-multiplicativity-v-free","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/block-multiplicativity-v-free.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.blockFactorProduct_neutron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.blockFactorProduct_neutron","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BlockMultiplicativityVFree.lean#L76-L83","doc":"The block-factor product at a free neutron (Z = 0, N = 1):\nblockFactorProduct v_p v_n 0 1 = v_n.\n**Verified** unconditionally. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.blockFactorProduct_proton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.blockFactorProduct_proton","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BlockMultiplicativityVFree.lean#L67-L74","doc":"The block-factor product at a free nucleon (Z = 1, N = 0):\nblockFactorProduct v_p v_n 1 0 = v_p.\n**Verified** unconditionally. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.blockFactorProduct_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.blockFactorProduct_add","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BlockMultiplicativityVFree.lean#L52-L65","doc":"The block-factor product is multiplicative in (Z, N).\n\nblockFactorProduct v_p v_n (Z + Z') (N + N')\n= blockFactorProduct v_p v_n Z N * blockFactorProduct v_p v_n Z' N'.\n\n**Verified** unconditionally via pow_add. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.blockFactorProduct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.blockFactorProduct","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BlockMultiplicativityVFree.lean#L39-L50","doc":"The block-factor product: v_p^Z · v_n^N for an atom\nwith Z protons and N neutrons.\n\nEmpirically (from binding-via-interface-knot.witness.json):\n  v_p ≈ 0.7084, v_n ≈ 0.6005 at q_0.\n\nDefined as a `noncomputable def` over a generic commutative\nring R; specialises to ℝ at q = q_0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instInhabitedNucleonFlavor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instInhabitedNucleonFlavor","kind":"instance","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BlockMultiplicativityVFree.lean#L37-L37","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instInhabitedNucleonFlavor.default","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instInhabitedNucleonFlavor.default","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BlockMultiplicativityVFree.lean#L37-L37","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instDecidableEqNucleonFlavor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instDecidableEqNucleonFlavor","kind":"instance","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BlockMultiplicativityVFree.lean#L37-L37","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.NucleonFlavor.neutron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.NucleonFlavor.neutron","kind":"ctor","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BlockMultiplicativityVFree.lean#L36-L36","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.NucleonFlavor.proton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.NucleonFlavor.proton","kind":"ctor","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BlockMultiplicativityVFree.lean#L35-L35","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.NucleonFlavor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.NucleonFlavor","kind":"inductive","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BlockMultiplicativityVFree.lean#L33-L37","doc":"Flavor of a nucleon block. ","signatureChunk":0}]}